# DO NOT create a .env at the repo root — nothing reads it.
# Each app loads ONLY its own env file (which is why separate Vercel
# projects work: each project sees just its own Root Directory):
#
#   Backend:  copy backend/.env.example → backend/.env.local, fill in secrets.
#     PORT, MONGODB_URL (or MONGO_URI), CLIENT_URL, JWT_SECRET, JWT_EXPIRES_IN.
#   Frontend: copy frontend/.env.example → frontend/.env.local, fill in secrets.
#     VITE_API_URL (empty = local Vite proxy), VITE_PORT.
#
# On Vercel, .env* files are gitignored and never deploy — set the same keys
# as Environment Variables in EACH project's dashboard, then redeploy.
# (Vite bakes VITE_* in at build time, so the frontend needs a rebuild
# after any VITE_API_URL change.)
